<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $10.7 bln in July 14 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $10.7 bln in July 14 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $10.7 billion in the July 14 week to $3,926.1 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $3.0 billion to $5,138.1 billion. M-1 was down $9.0 billion to $1,057.4 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,927.6 billion versus $3,924.7 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
